// Signing for CI, applied through XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE in .github/workflows/build.yml.
//
// project.yml keeps the historical CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY "Transcriber Dev", which exists for
// exactly one reason: macOS binds microphone and audio-capture grants to a signature, so a
// stable certificate keeps TCC grants alive across rebuilds (scripts/make-signing-cert.sh).
// A runner holds no grants and records nothing, so the reason does not reach it. Importing a
// private key into CI would be a real secret stored for no benefit at all.
//
// Overriding here rather than in project.yml or scripts/check.sh is what keeps the gate one
// thing: CI runs the script a developer runs, and only the signature differs. Verified on
// Xcode 26.6 — an ad-hoc host still accepts the injected test bundle, because the two agree
// on having no team identity rather than on sharing one.
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
